  const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`);
  if (!res.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Failed to load profile: ${res.status}`);
  }
  const profile = await res.json();
  return profile.name.toUpperCase();
}
```

In this corrected form, the fetch is awaited, the response status is validated, and errors are permitted to flow upward to the calling code rather than being suppressed.

